.TH AGENT-SANDBOX-EXEC 1 "2026-06-30" "agent-sandbox-exec 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-sandbox-exec \- run a command inside the BPF-LSM agent sandbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-sandbox-exec
.RB [ -h ]
.RB [ -V ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-sandbox-exec
runs
.I command
(and its arguments) inside the agent sandbox: the process and every process it
spawns is migrated into the agent cgroup
.RI ( /sys/fs/cgroup/agent-sandbox-exec ),
where a BPF-LSM program on the
.I file_open
hook blocks opens of the files listed in
.IR /etc/agent-sandbox-exec/denylist ,
returning
.BR ENOENT .
.PP
This defeats read-via-delegation \(em
.BR "cat secret | \&..." ,
hardlinks to a secret, and
.B "cp secret"
are all blocked, because the source
.B open
is denied.
.PP
No mount or user namespace is created, so the command sees the real environment
\(em real mount table, real
.I /dev
ownership, real supplementary groups, real
.I /proc
\(em and can still troubleshoot kernel and system issues accurately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENT_SANDBOX_INSECURE=1
Run
.I command
.B unsandboxed
(no protection). Takes precedence over everything else.
.TP
.B AGENT_SANDBOX_CGROUP
Override the agent cgroup path (default
.IR /sys/fs/cgroup/agent-sandbox-exec ).
.TP
.B AGENT_SANDBOX_REQ
Override the migration request directory (default
.IR /run/agent-sandbox-exec/req ).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The command ran and exited 0.
.TP
.B 2
The sandbox was not ready, migration timed out (is
.B agent-sandbox-execd
running?), or no command was given. The command was
.I not
executed.
.TP
.I *
Otherwise the command's own exit status.
.SH "FAIL-CLOSED BEHAVIOUR"
If
.B agent-sandbox-execd
is not running, the command is
.I not
execited (exit 2). The launcher never runs a command unprotected unless
.B AGENT_SANDBOX_INSECURE=1
is set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/agent-sandbox-exec/denylist
The list of secret files to block \(em see
.BR agent-sandbox-exec-denylist (5).
.TP
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/agent-sandbox-exec
The agent cgroup.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR agent-sandbox-exec-denylist (5),
.BR agent-sandbox-execd (8),
.BR systemctl (1).
